    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "By the in-ter-ces-sions of Thy Mar-tyrs, O Lord, grant rest un-to the souls of Thy ser-vants.\n\nTheir ar-dent hope made the choirs of Mar-tyrs strong; hope gave them wings to soar un-to Thy love with a fier-y zeal, in their souls pre-fig-ur-ing the fu-ture rest which nev-er can be shak-en, which do Thou gra-cious-ly vouch-safe the de-part-ed faith-ful to in-her-it, O Su-preme-ly__ Good.__\n\nTheir souls shall dwell a-mong good__ things.\n\nBe pleased that those who have passed from hence in faith at-tain to Thy di-vine il-lu-mi-na-tion more bright than light, and since Thou a-lone, O Christ, art mer-ci-ful, give them rest in the bos-om of Fa-ther A-bra-ham, ac-count--ing them wor-thy of the ev-er-last-ing bless-ed--ness.__\n\nGlo-ry to the Fa-ther, and to the Son, and to the Ho--ly Spir-it.\n\nThou art by na-ture com-pas-sion-ate and kind, Thou Who de-sir-est mer-cy: Grant to those whom Thou hast con-veyed from this place of mis-er-y and shad-ow of death that they might be es-tab-lished there where Thy light doth shine, O Sav--iour, since Thou art the A-byss of all__ com-pas-sion.\n\nBoth now and ev--er, and un-to the ag--es of ag-es. A-men.\n\nO_ blame-less Maid, we know thee to be an ark, most ho-ly tab-er-nac--le, and tab-let of the law of grace, for through thee for-give-ness hath been giv-en to those jus-ti-fied and de-liv-ered through the pure Blood of Him Who re-ceived a bod-y from thy womb, O pure and spot-less__ one.__\n\nIt is not pos-si-ble for man to see God, on Whom the or--ders of An-gels dare not gaze. But through thee, O Vir-gin, the in-car-nate Word clear-ly ap-peared to mor-tals. Hence, with the Heav-ens’ hosts, we mag--ni-fy Him as we all call thee bless-ed as is__ right.___"
    }
  }
